# Copy to .env.local and fill in your StabiFlow Supabase project's values
# (Project Settings -> API in the Supabase dashboard). Never commit the
# real .env.local - it's gitignored.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# --- Edge function secrets (set via `supabase secrets set`, never in this file) ---
# SUPABASE_URL
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
# SOCIAL_CRON_SECRET               - shared secret the scheduler cron uses to call the publish worker
# SOCIAL_AUTO_PUBLISH_ENABLED      - environment-level emergency kill switch for automatic publishing (see docs/architecture/multi-tenancy.md)
#
# --- Integrations module (Phase C) ---
# INTEGRATIONS_META_APP_ID              - the StabiFlow Meta App's client id (developers.facebook.com)
# INTEGRATIONS_META_APP_SECRET          - the StabiFlow Meta App's client secret; also used to verify WhatsApp webhook signatures (X-Hub-Signature-256)
# INTEGRATIONS_META_GRAPH_API_VERSION   - e.g. v21.0
# INTEGRATIONS_META_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI  - must exactly match a Valid OAuth Redirect URI configured on the Meta App: <SUPABASE_URL>/functions/v1/integrations-oauth-callback
# INTEGRATIONS_APP_ORIGIN               - StabiFlow's own frontend origin the OAuth callback redirects back to (never derived from the request - see integrations-oauth-callback's header comment)
# INTEGRATIONS_META_MOCK_MODE           - "true" ONLY in development, when no real Meta App is configured yet; fabricates resources instead of calling Graph. Must be unset/false in production.
# WHATSAPP_WEBHOOK_VERIFY_TOKEN         - the token entered in the Meta App dashboard's WhatsApp webhook subscription (verification handshake)
#
# Per-workspace Meta/WhatsApp tokens are NOT environment variables in
# StabiFlow - they live in Supabase Vault, one per workspace_integrations
# row, and are only ever read server-side via
# get_workspace_integration_secret() (service_role only). See
# docs/architecture/multi-tenancy.md.
